## 13. What does "physics are broken" actually mean?

Pick your preferred direction, or combine them.

### A. 🌀 Spatial anomalies

Certain star systems don't obey normal spatial rules.

Examples:

·         two systems are physically adjacent despite being light-years apart

·         ships disappear during jumps

·         stations appear in impossible locations

·         routes change

·         a system can only be reached under specific conditions

### B. ⏳ Time anomalies

Some regions don't obey normal time.

Examples:

·         ships return years later

·         someone encounters their own wreck

·         messages arrive before they are sent

·         an entire colony experiences time differently

### C. 🧲 Fundamental physics anomalies

Gravity, energy, matter or causality behave differently.

Examples:

·         planets orbit impossible objects

·         weapons behave differently in certain systems

·         ships experience impossible acceleration

·         matter appears/disappears

### D. 🏗️ Someone/something is deliberately manipulating physics

The anomalies aren't natural.

Something built the system.

Possibilities:

·         ancient civilization

·         AI

·         experimental technology

·         unknown intelligence

### E. 🌌 Reality itself is unstable

The universe isn't behaving according to one consistent set of laws.

This is the **biggest and strangest option**.

