**Highest-leverage action for the next 30 minutes:** lock the **campaign spine and branch architecture**, not individual dialogue. I recommend a **branch-and-bottleneck structure**: major choices genuinely change factions, NPCs, missions and galaxy state, but the story periodically reconverges so development does not explode into hundreds of bespoke missions. That is the same production logic used in effective choice-driven narrative systems. ([GameDesign.gg][1])

