The cleanest version of the story is actually this:

> **Humanity believes it lives inside a normal galaxy. It doesn't.**
>
> Spatial anomalies occasionally expose relationships that exist underneath humanity's conventional map.
>
> An ancient civilization discovered this phenomenon before humanity did. They studied it, eventually realized it was becoming dangerous, and constructed containment systems.
>
> They failed and disappeared.
>
> Humanity eventually rediscovered the same phenomenon.
>
> The player's ship is somehow entangled with it.
>
> By the end of Campaign 1, the player discovers that the "galaxy" humanity knows is an artificial spatial construct.
>
> **But nobody knows who created it, why it exists, or what is outside it.**

That is coherent.

